{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6vCQyT8HV6qQmnwad4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `cachelib/lru.py` to the spec and added 10 tests in `tests/test_lru.py`. All 10 pass.\n\nIt stores each entry as `(value, expires_at)` in an `OrderedDict`, so every operation is O(1) on average.\n\n- **Expiry:** an entry expires when the clock reaches its expiry time, so with `ttl=10` it is gone at exactly 10. An expired `get` counts as a miss and an expiration, never an eviction. Calling `put` on an existing key restarts its TTL.\n- **`__contains__`:** it doesn't change recency, and it removes an expired entry it finds. That removal also counts as an expiration, which the spec doesn't say either way.\n- **Eviction:** when the cache goes over capacity, `put` evicts the least recently used entry. It doesn't look for expired entries to drop first, so an expired entry that nobody has touched can still be evicted in place of a live one.\n\nThe tests use a fake clock and cover:\n\n- the capacity check\n- eviction order\n- `get` and update refreshing recency\n- `delete`\n- TTL expiry through `get` and `contains`\n- the stats counters\n\nI didn't commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2980,"cache_read_input_tokens":26438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2980},"output_tokens":392,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d540151d-861e-4da0-8de9-8161c9d4787e","uuid":"888d5937-9108-48c0-8c9d-524874907ea5","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:02:47.000Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6vC1epAP7FeJg5bwPU"}
